<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Æthelbald of Mercia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/757">757</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Æthelbald was king of Mercia from 716 to 757 and the dominant ruler of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> for much of his reign. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bede">Bede</a> counted all the English kingdoms south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humber">Humber</a> as subject to him by 731, and a charter of 736 styles him king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>. Boniface rebuked him for his treatment of the church, and he was murdered by his own bodyguard at Seckington in 757, to be succeeded after a brief struggle by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/offa-of-mercia">Offa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aethelbald-of-mercia.jpg" alt="Æthelbald of Mercia" width="320" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Poliphilo · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Repton_Stone-_detail.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the 8th century <b>Æthelbald</b> and Offa fought the Welsh kingdoms and compelled the southern kingdoms to accept their lordship.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-mercia">Kingdom of Mercia · Military</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in Seckington, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-kingdom">the United Kingdom</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=52.66,-1.62&amp;year=747" aria-label="Seckington on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4514 348 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Æthelbald of Mercia"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4964 618h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4964 618h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=52.66,-1.62&amp;year=747">What was here in 747 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
